## The owner's rules — checked before the render

- [ ] The title card from frame 0, no longer than 1.5 s; the final frame held at least 60 frames; 18 to 22 s in all.
- [ ] Every event but the hold changes the picture; the hold changes nothing.
- [ ] The video follows the scrolly's picture and choreography, without its cards.
- [ ] A documentary argument — transform, magnify, morph — not marks toggled on.
- [ ] As little text as the picture allows: no sentence, no standfirst; a close-up names only what it frames.
- [ ] A close-up centres its subject on both axes.
- [ ] No end card: the video ends on its picture, the credit on one line.
- [ ] No word under the type floor at any event's end; every word drawn at its measured width.
- [ ] ONE art direction, composed from the newsroom's identity (NEWSROOM.md) — never the three filed demo directions.
- [ ] Every word in the language named above, that language chosen by the first rule that answers.
- [ ] The no-break space written as the `\u00A0` escape in the scripts, never typed.
- [ ] Looked at before the mp4: every event's last frame and the middle of each gesture.

